  "goodToKnow": "Betrübt means sad or saddened, a slightly elevated word: tief betrübt, betrübt dreinschauen (to look downcast). Betrüben means to sadden: Das betrübt mich sehr. From trüb (cloudy, gloomy). Don't confuse it with betrügen (to cheat). Goethe's line himmelhoch jauchzend, zum Tode betrübt (on top of the world, then in the depths of despair) from Egmont is still quoted for mood swings."
